<title>USA: Kleinwort Benson cuts Chile, recommends Brazil.</title>
<headline>Kleinwort Benson cuts Chile, recommends Brazil.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dresdner Kleinwort Benson on Thursday urged an underweight position on Chile and recommended Brazil in its model portfolio of Latin American stocks.</p>
<p>&quot;Chile is bouncing back on the imminent prospect of lower interest rates,&quot; London analysts Joe MacHatton and Rui Antunes wrote in a report released in New York.</p>
<p>&quot;This is time to thank the market, sell some stock, and go to an underweighting in this overpriced, slow-earnings-growth market,&quot; they said. &quot;Put the money into Brazil, where valuations are more attractive and growth is more rapid.&quot;  </p>
<p>MacHatton and Antunes said investors should sell or trim Chilean investments in Sociedad Quimica y Minera de Chile, Empresa Nacional de Electricidad and Embotelladora Andina.</p>
<p>Recommended Brazilian stocks include Eletrobras, Cosipa and Telebras.</p>
<p>((-- Ian Simpson, Wall Street Desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
